    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the balance thing, but that's hard to actually do in a classroom. some people argue that if you focus too much on the \"injustices\" part, it just makes kids feel guilty or divided rather than proud of their country. on the other hand, people who want the systemic justice focus say that the \"triumphs\" version is basically just propaganda that ignores the truth. in your opinion, which of those two views is actually more grounded in how history really works?",
